ablar en público me saca de mi zona de confort.","difficulty":1,"tags":["personal-growth","collocations"]},{"id":"en-give-it-a-try","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u09","text":"give it a try","translation_es":"probar / intentarlo","accepted_translations":["probar","intentarlo","hacer la prueba"],"ipa":"/ˈɡɪv ɪt ə ˈtraɪ/","romanization":null,"emoji":"👍","example_en":"You've never tried yoga? Give it a try!","example_es":"¿Nunca probaste yoga? ¡Probalo!","difficulty":1,"tags":["personal-growth","collocations"]},{"id":"en-debate","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"debate","translation_es":"debate","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/dɪˈbeɪt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🎤","example_en":"We had a debate about social media.","example_es":"Tuvimos un debate sobre las redes sociales.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument"]},{"id":"en-moreover","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"moreover","translation_es":"además (formal)","accepted_translations":["además"],"ipa":"/mɔrˈoʊvər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"➕","example_en":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","example_es":"El plan es barato. Además, es fácil de empezar.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-furthermore","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"furthermore","translation_es":"asimismo / es más","accepted_translations":["asimismo","es más"],"ipa":"/ˈfɜrðərˌmɔr/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Furthermore, free education gives everyone the same chances.","example_es":"Asimismo, la educación gratuita da a todos las mismas oportunidades.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-as-a-result","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"as a result","translation_es":"como resultado / por eso","accepted_translations":["como resultado","en consecuencia"],"ipa":"/æz ə rɪˈzʌlt/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"It rained all week. As a result, the match was canceled.","example_es":"Llovió toda la semana. Como resultado, se canceló el partido.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-what-matters-is","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"what matters is","translation_es":"lo que importa es","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/wʌt ˈmætərz ɪz/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"What matters is that you tried.","example_es":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste.","difficulty":1,"tags":["cleft-sentences"]},{"id":"en-the-reason-why","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"the reason why","translation_es":"la razón por la que","accepted_translations":["el motivo por el que"],"ipa":"/ðə ˈrizən waɪ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"The reason why I called is that I need your help.","example_es":"La razón por la que llamé es que necesito tu ayuda.","difficulty":1,"tags":["cleft-sentences"]},{"id":"en-in-other-words","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"in other words","translation_es":"en otras palabras / es decir","accepted_translations":["en otras palabras","es decir","o sea"],"ipa":"/ɪn ˈʌðər ˈwɜrdz/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"He was late again. In other words, he does not care.","example_es":"Llegó tarde otra vez. En otras palabras, no le importa.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-admittedly","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"admittedly","translation_es":"es cierto que / hay que reconocer que","accepted_translations":["es cierto que","hay que reconocer que"],"ipa":"/ədˈmɪtɪdli/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Admittedly, it is expensive.","example_es":"Es cierto que es caro.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-nevertheless","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"nevertheless","translation_es":"aun así / de todos modos","accepted_translations":["aun así","de todos modos","no obstante"],"ipa":"/ˌnɛvərðəˈlɛs/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"It was difficult. Nevertheless, we finished on time.","example_es":"Fue difícil. Aun así, terminamos a tiempo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-on-the-contrary","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"on the contrary","translation_es":"al contrario","accepted_translations":["por el contrario"],"ipa":"/ɑn ðə ˈkɑnˌtrɛri/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🔄","example_en":"I'm not tired. On the contrary, I feel great.","example_es":"No estoy cansado. Al contrario, me siento genial.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-point-of-view","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"point of view","translation_es":"punto de vista","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈpɔɪnt əv ˈvju/","romanization":null,"emoji":"👁️","example_en":"I understand your point of view, but I disagree.","example_es":"Entiendo tu punto de vista, pero no estoy de acuerdo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument"]},{"id":"en-valid","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"valid","translation_es":"válido","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈvælɪd/","romanization":null,"emoji":"✔️","example_en":"That's a valid point.","example_es":"Es un argumento válido.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","adjectives"]},{"id":"en-convincing","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"convincing","translation_es":"convincente","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/kənˈvɪnsɪŋ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Her argument was very convincing.","example_es":"Su argumento fue muy convincente.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","adjectives"]},{"id":"en-assumption","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"assumption","translation_es":"suposición / supuesto","accepted_translations":["suposición","supuesto"],"ipa":"/əˈsʌmpʃən/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"That's just an assumption. Where is the evidence?","example_es":"Eso es sólo una suposición. ¿Dónde están las pruebas?","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument"]},{"id":"en-take-into-account","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"take into account","translation_es":"tener en cuenta","accepted_translations":["tomar en cuenta"],"ipa":"/ˈteɪk ˈɪntu əˈkaʊnt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🧮","example_en":"We need to take the costs into account.","example_es":"Tenemos que tener en cuenta los costos.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","collocations"]},{"id":"en-outweigh","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"outweigh","translation_es":"superar / pesar más que","accepted_translations":["superar","pesar más que"],"ipa":"/aʊtˈweɪ/","romanization":null,"emoji":"⚖️","example_en":"The benefits outweigh the costs.","example_es":"Los beneficios superan a los costos.","difficulty":1,"tags":["argument","verbs"]},{"id":"en-to-sum-up","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"to sum up","translation_es":"en resumen / para resumir","accepted_translations":["en resumen","para resumir","en síntesis"],"ipa":"/tə ˈsʌm ˈʌp/","romanization":null,"emoji":"📝","example_en":"To sum up, I think the plan is a good idea.","example_es":"En resumen, creo que el plan es una buena idea.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-all-things-considered","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u10","text":"all things considered","translation_es":"después de todo / en definitiva","accepted_translations":["después de todo","en definitiva","considerando todo"],"ipa":"/ˈɔl ˈθɪŋz kənˈsɪdərd/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"All things considered, it was a good year.","example_es":"En definitiva, fue un buen año.","difficulty":1,"tags":["connectors","argument"]},{"id":"en-novel","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"novel","translation_es":"novela","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈnɑvəl/","romanization":null,"emoji":"📖","example_en":"I could not stop reading the novel.","example_es":"No podía dejar de leer la novela.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-plot","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"plot","translation_es":"trama / argumento","accepted_translations":["trama","argumento"],"ipa":"/plɑt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🧵","example_en":"The plot is clever and surprising.","example_es":"La trama es ingeniosa y sorprendente.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-character","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"character","translation_es":"personaje","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈkærəktər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🎭","example_en":"My favorite character is the old fisherman.","example_es":"Mi personaje favorito es el viejo pescador.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-chapter","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"chapter","translation_es":"capítulo","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈtʃæptər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🔖","example_en":"The twist is in the last chapter.","example_es":"El giro está en el último capítulo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-narrator","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"narrator","translation_es":"narrador / narradora","accepted_translations":["narrador","narradora"],"ipa":"/ˈnærˌeɪtər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🗨️","example_en":"The narrator was lying to us.","example_es":"La narradora nos estaba mintiendo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-twist","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"twist","translation_es":"giro (inesperado)","accepted_translations":["giro","vuelta de tuerca"],"ipa":"/twɪst/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🌀","example_en":"I didn't expect that twist at the end.","example_es":"No me esperaba ese giro al final.","difficulty":1,"tags":["literature"]},{"id":"en-turn-out","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"turn out","translation_es":"resultar","accepted_translations":["resultar que"],"ipa":"/ˈtɜrn ˈaʊt/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"It turned out that we lived on the same street.","example_es":"Resultó que vivíamos en la misma calle.","difficulty":1,"tags":["narrative","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"en-set-off","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"set off","translation_es":"salir / ponerse en camino","accepted_translations":["salir","ponerse en camino","partir"],"ipa":"/ˈsɛt ˈɔf/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🚶","example_en":"We set off early in the morning.","example_es":"Salimos temprano a la mañana.","difficulty":1,"tags":["narrative","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"en-out-of-the-blue","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"out of the blue","translation_es":"de la nada / de repente","accepted_translations":["de la nada","de repente","sin aviso"],"ipa":"/ˈaʊt əv ðə ˈblu/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🔵","example_en":"My old friend called me out of the blue.","example_es":"Mi viejo amigo me llamó de la nada.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms"]},{"id":"en-break-the-ice","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"break the ice","translation_es":"romper el hielo","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈbreɪk ðə ˈaɪs/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🧊","example_en":"A good joke can break the ice.","example_es":"Un buen chiste puede romper el hielo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms"]},{"id":"en-burst-into-tears","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"burst into tears","translation_es":"ponerse a llorar / romper en llanto","accepted_translations":["ponerse a llorar","romper en llanto"],"ipa":"/ˈbɜrst ˈɪntu ˈtɪrz/","romanization":null,"emoji":"😭","example_en":"When she heard the news, she burst into tears.","example_es":"Cuando escuchó la noticia, se puso a llorar.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms","emotions"]},{"id":"en-never-had","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"never had","translation_es":"nunca había (inversión)","accepted_translations":["nunca había"],"ipa":"/ˈnɛvər hæd/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Never had she felt so alone.","example_es":"Nunca se había sentido tan sola.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion"]},{"id":"en-hardly","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"hardly","translation_es":"apenas","accepted_translations":["casi no"],"ipa":"/ˈhɑrdli/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Hardly had she stopped when the door opened.","example_es":"Apenas se había detenido cuando se abrió la puerta.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion","adverbs"]},{"id":"en-no-sooner","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"no sooner","translation_es":"no bien / en cuanto","accepted_translations":["no bien","en cuanto"],"ipa":"/noʊ ˈsunər/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"No sooner had we arrived than it started to rain.","example_es":"No bien llegamos, empezó a llover.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion"]},{"id":"en-little-did-i-know","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"little did I know","translation_es":"poco me imaginaba / no tenía idea","accepted_translations":["poco me imaginaba","no tenía idea"],"ipa":"/ˈlɪtəl dɪd aɪ ˈnoʊ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Little did I know that she would become my wife.","example_es":"Poco me imaginaba que iba a ser mi esposa.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion"]},{"id":"en-a-piece-of-cake","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"a piece of cake","translation_es":"pan comido / muy fácil","accepted_translations":["pan comido","muy fácil"],"ipa":"/ə ˈpis əv ˈkeɪk/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🍰","example_en":"The exam was a piece of cake.","example_es":"El examen fue pan comido.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms"]},{"id":"en-once-in-a-blue-moon","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"once in a blue moon","translation_es":"muy de vez en cuando","accepted_translations":["de vez en cuando","casi nunca"],"ipa":"/ˈwʌns ɪn ə ˈblu ˈmun/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🌕","example_en":"I only go to the cinema once in a blue moon.","example_es":"Voy al cine muy de vez en cuando.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms"]},{"id":"en-the-last-straw","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u11","text":"the last straw","translation_es":"la gota que rebalsó el vaso","accepted_translations":["la gota que colmó el vaso"],"ipa":"/ðə ˈlæst ˈstrɔ/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🥤","example_en":"The noise at three in the morning was the last straw.","example_es":"El ruido a las tres de la mañana fue la gota que rebalsó el vaso.","difficulty":1,"tags":["idioms"]},{"id":"en-dilemma","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"dilemma","translation_es":"dilema","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/dɪˈlɛmə/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🤔","example_en":"I've got a real dilemma.","example_es":"Tengo un verdadero dilema.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions"]},{"id":"en-weigh-up","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"weigh up","translation_es":"sopesar / evaluar","accepted_translations":["sopesar","evaluar"],"ipa":"/ˈweɪ ˈʌp/","romanization":null,"emoji":"⚖️","example_en":"I am weighing up the pros and cons.","example_es":"Estoy sopesando los pros y los contras.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"en-pros-and-cons","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"pros and cons","translation_es":"pros y contras","accepted_translations":["ventajas y desventajas"],"ipa":"/ˈproʊz ən ˈkɑnz/","romanization":null,"emoji":"📋","example_en":"Write down the pros and cons.","example_es":"Anotá los pros y los contras.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions","collocations"]},{"id":"en-trade-off","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"trade-off","translation_es":"concesión / costo a cambio","accepted_translations":["costo a cambio","equilibrio"],"ipa":"/ˈtreɪd ˌɔf/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"More money, less free time: that is the trade-off.","example_es":"Más plata, menos tiempo libre: ése es el costo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions"]},{"id":"en-gut-feeling","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"gut feeling","translation_es":"corazonada / intuición","accepted_translations":["corazonada","intuición","presentimiento"],"ipa":"/ˈɡʌt ˌfilɪŋ/","romanization":null,"emoji":"💭","example_en":"My gut feeling says I should go.","example_es":"Mi intuición me dice que tengo que ir.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions","collocations"]},{"id":"en-have-second-thoughts","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"have second thoughts","translation_es":"dudar / replantearse algo","accepted_translations":["dudar","replantearse","pensarlo dos veces"],"ipa":"/ˈhæv ˈsɛkənd ˈθɔts/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"I'm having second thoughts about the trip.","example_es":"Estoy dudando sobre el viaje.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions","collocations"]},{"id":"en-at-stake","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"at stake","translation_es":"en juego","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/æt ˈsteɪk/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🎲","example_en":"A big client is at stake.","example_es":"Hay un cliente importante en juego.","difficulty":1,"tags":["decisions","collocations"]},{"id":"en-conflict","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"conflict","translation_es":"conflicto","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈkɑnflɪkt/","romanization":null,"emoji":"⚡","example_en":"There has been a conflict between the two teams.","example_es":"Hubo un conflicto entre los dos equipos.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict"]},{"id":"en-resolve","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"resolve","translation_es":"resolver / solucionar (un conflicto)","accepted_translations":["resolver un conflicto","zanjar"],"ipa":"/rɪˈzɑlv/","romanization":null,"emoji":"✅","example_en":"We can help you resolve the conflict.","example_es":"Podemos ayudarte a resolver el conflicto.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict","verbs"]},{"id":"en-mediator","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"mediator","translation_es":"mediador / mediadora","accepted_translations":["mediador","mediadora"],"ipa":"/ˈmidiˌeɪtər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🕊️","example_en":"A mediator helps both sides listen to each other.","example_es":"Un mediador ayuda a las dos partes a escucharse.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict"]},{"id":"en-take-sides","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"take sides","translation_es":"tomar partido","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈteɪk ˈsaɪdz/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"I don't want to take sides in their argument.","example_es":"No quiero tomar partido en su pelea.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict","collocations"]},{"id":"en-common-ground","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"common ground","translation_es":"puntos en común","accepted_translations":["terreno común"],"ipa":"/ˈkɑmən ˈɡraʊnd/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🤝","example_en":"Try to find some common ground.","example_es":"Tratá de encontrar puntos en común.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict","collocations"]},{"id":"en-stand-up-for","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"stand up for","translation_es":"defender (a alguien o algo)","accepted_translations":["defender","dar la cara por"],"ipa":"/ˈstænd ˈʌp fɔr/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🛡️","example_en":"I have to stand up for my team.","example_es":"Tengo que defender a mi equipo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"en-back-down","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"back down","translation_es":"ceder / echarse atrás","accepted_translations":["echarse atrás","dar el brazo a torcer"],"ipa":"/ˈbæk ˈdaʊn/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Neither side wanted to back down.","example_es":"Ninguna de las dos partes quería ceder.","difficulty":1,"tags":["conflict","phrasal-verbs"]},{"id":"en-not-only","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"not only","translation_es":"no sólo","accepted_translations":["no solamente"],"ipa":"/nɑt ˈoʊnli/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Not only is the service free, but it is also confidential.","example_es":"El servicio no sólo es gratuito, sino que también es confidencial.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion","connectors"]},{"id":"en-under-no-circumstances","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"under no circumstances","translation_es":"bajo ninguna circunstancia","accepted_translations":["de ninguna manera"],"ipa":"/ˈʌndər ˈnoʊ ˈsɜrkəmˌstænsɪz/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🚫","example_en":"Under no circumstances should you open this door.","example_es":"Bajo ninguna circunstancia deberías abrir esta puerta.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion"]},{"id":"en-only-then","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"only then","translation_es":"sólo entonces","accepted_translations":["recién entonces"],"ipa":"/ˈoʊnli ˈðɛn/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Only then can we finish on time.","example_es":"Sólo entonces podremos terminar a tiempo.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion"]},{"id":"en-should-you","language_code":"en","unit_id":"b2-u12","text":"should you","translation_es":"si llegaras a / en caso de que (formal)","accepted_translations":["si llegaras a","en caso de que"],"ipa":"/ˈʃʊd ju/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Should you need help, please call reception.","example_es":"Si necesita ayuda, llame a recepción.","difficulty":1,"tags":["inversion","conditionals"]}],"lessons":[{"id":"b2-u01-l01","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":1,"title_es":"No quise decir eso","objective_es":"Aclarar un malentendido y explicar lo que quisiste decir.","intro":{"explanation":"Cuando algo se entiende mal, en inglés aclarás la intención con mean to: I didn’t mean to sound rude (no fue mi intención). Actually corrige una idea equivocada: Actually, I wasn’t angry (en realidad). Un misunderstanding es un malentendido y el tone, el tono de lo que decís.","examples":[{"target":"I didn't mean to sound rude.","base":"No fue mi intención sonar maleducado."},{"target":"It wasn't an argument, just a misunderstanding.","base":"No fue una pelea, sólo un malentendido."}]},"takeaways":["Aclarás tu intención con I didn’t mean to…","Corregís una idea equivocada con actually."]},{"id":"b2-u01-l02","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":2,"title_es":"Leer entre líneas","objective_es":"Entender indirectas, sarcasmo y lo que alguien da a entender.","intro":{"explanation":"No todo se dice de forma directa. Imply es dar a entender algo sin decirlo; to drop a hint es tirar una indirecta. Si alguien es sarcastic, dice lo contrario de lo que piensa. Apparently (al parecer) y seem (parecer) muestran que no estás del todo seguro.","examples":[{"target":"Are you implying that I am lazy?","base":"¿Estás insinuando que soy vago?"},{"target":"Apparently, she was talking about Tom.","base":"Al parecer, hablaba de Tom."}]},"takeaways":["Reconocés una indirecta y el sarcasmo.","Contás lo que no sabés seguro con apparently y seem."]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «No quise decir eso» y «Leer entre líneas».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l03","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":4,"title_es":"Recordar, dejar, intentar","objective_es":"Usar remember, forget, stop, try y regret con -ing o con infinitivo.","intro":{"explanation":"Con -ing hablás de algo que ya hiciste o de la actividad misma: I remember meeting her (me acuerdo de haberla conocido), I regret saying it (me arrepiento de haberlo dicho), We stopped talking (dejamos de hablar). Con to + verbo hablás de lo que hay que hacer o del propósito: Remember to call (acordate de llamar), We stopped to talk (paramos para hablar). Try + -ing es probar algo; try to, intentar.","examples":[{"target":"I remember meeting her, but I forgot to ask her name.","base":"Me acuerdo de haberla conocido, pero me olvidé de preguntarle el nombre."},{"target":"I regret saying those things to my brother.","base":"Me arrepiento de haberle dicho esas cosas a mi hermano."}]},"takeaways":["Distinguís remember doing (ya pasó) de remember to do (hay que hacerlo).","Usás stop, try y regret con el sentido correcto."]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":5,"title_es":"Directo, pero con tacto","objective_es":"Decir algo difícil de forma clara y amable.","intro":{"explanation":"Straightforward es claro y directo (algo bueno); blunt es tan directo que puede ofender; tactful es tener tacto. Para señalar un problema usás point out, y para sacar un tema, bring up. Tend to (soler) suaviza una crítica: You tend to interrupt people suena mejor que You always interrupt.","examples":[{"target":"She pointed out a mistake in my report.","base":"Señaló un error en mi informe."},{"target":"People tend to speak faster when they are nervous.","base":"La gente tiende a hablar más rápido cuando está nerviosa."}]},"takeaways":["Distinguís straightforward, blunt y tactful.","Señalás un problema con point out y lo suavizás con tend to."]},{"id":"b2-u01-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Recordar, dejar, intentar» y «Directo, pero con tacto».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l05","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":7,"title_es":"Más allá de las palabras","objective_es":"Interpretar el lenguaje corporal y suavizar lo que decís.","intro":{"explanation":"El body language (lenguaje corporal) también comunica. Para hablar de lo que ves sin afirmarlo: He seems nervous, She tends to look away. Para suavizar una opinión: I’d say…, It seems to me that…, a bit. Y si no se entendió tu idea: I couldn’t get my point across.","examples":[{"target":"His body language showed that he was nervous.","base":"Su lenguaje corporal mostraba que estaba nervioso."},{"target":"It is hard to get your ideas across in a short message.","base":"Es difícil transmitir tus ideas en un mensaje corto."}]},"takeaways":["Describís el lenguaje corporal con seem y tend to.","Suavizás una opinión y explicás si una idea no se entendió."]},{"id":"b2-u01-listen","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-words","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-final","unit_id":"b2-u01","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Decir las cosas con matices».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l01","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":1,"title_es":"Sentarse a negociar","objective_es":"Presentar una propuesta, negociar un precio y cerrar un trato.","intro":{"explanation":"Para negociar: negotiate a price (negociar un precio), make a proposal (hacer una propuesta) y, al final, reach an agreement (llegar a un acuerdo). We have a deal significa trato hecho. Para sugerir algo con suavidad, What if we…? va con el pasado: What if we kept the price?","examples":[{"target":"We need to negotiate a better price.","base":"Tenemos que negociar un mejor precio."},{"target":"If you agree, we have a deal.","base":"Si estás de acuerdo, trato hecho."}]},"takeaways":["Presentás y discutís una propuesta.","Cerrás una negociación: We have a deal, we reached an agreement."]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":2,"title_es":"Ceder un poco","objective_es":"Buscar un término medio y decir qué es lo más importante para vos.","intro":{"explanation":"En una negociación nadie consigue todo: a compromise es un término medio. Let’s meet halfway propone que los dos cedan un poco. Para explicar qué te importa más: Our main priority is… Y si podés adaptarte, sos flexible.","examples":[{"target":"You want ten, I want six. Let's meet halfway at eight.","base":"Vos querés diez y yo seis. Cedamos los dos: ocho."},{"target":"Our main priority is the customer.","base":"Nuestra prioridad principal es el cliente."}]},"takeaways":["Proponés un término medio: Let’s meet halfway.","Explicás tus prioridades y si podés ser flexible."]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Sentarse a negociar» y «Ceder un poco».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":4,"title_es":"Con una condición","objective_es":"Poner condiciones y precauciones con as long as, provided that, otherwise e in case.","intro":{"explanation":"As long as y provided that ponen una condición y van con presente: I’ll sign, provided that the price stays the same. Otherwise dice qué pasa si no se cumple. In case es una precaución: llevás un paraguas in case it rains (por si llueve, aunque no sepas si va a llover).","examples":[{"target":"You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully.","base":"Podés usar mi auto siempre que manejes con cuidado."},{"target":"Take an umbrella in case it rains.","base":"Llevá un paraguas por si llueve."}]},"takeaways":["Ponés condiciones con as long as y provided that.","Hablás de precauciones con in case y de consecuencias con otherwise."]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":5,"title_es":"Liderar un equipo","objective_es":"Repartir tareas, hablar de la carga de trabajo y convencer.","intro":{"explanation":"A leader no hace todo: delegate es delegar tareas en otros. Si tenés demasiado trabajo, tu workload es demasiado grande. Take on es asumir una tarea nueva. Persuade someone to do something es convencer a alguien de hacer algo.","examples":[{"target":"You should delegate some tasks to your team.","base":"Deberías delegar algunas tareas en tu equipo."},{"target":"She took on a new project last week.","base":"La semana pasada asumió un proyecto nuevo."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de la carga de trabajo y de asumir tareas nuevas.","Delegás y convencés con persuade."]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Con una condición» y «Liderar un equipo».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l05","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":7,"title_es":"Decir que no con cortesía","objective_es":"Rechazar una oferta o una tarea sin cerrar la puerta.","intro":{"explanation":"Turn down es rechazar (una oferta, una invitación, un trabajo). Para decir que no con cortesía, suavizás: I’m afraid I’ll have to turn it down (me temo que…), I’d love to, but… Y si querés seguir negociando, ofrecés una alternativa con as long as o provided that.","examples":[{"target":"He turned down the job because the salary was too low.","base":"Rechazó el trabajo porque el sueldo era muy bajo."},{"target":"I'm afraid I'll have to turn it down.","base":"Me temo que voy a tener que rechazarlo."}]},"takeaways":["Rechazás algo con cortesía: I’m afraid I’ll have to turn it down.","Ofrecés una alternativa con una condición."]},{"id":"b2-u02-listen","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-words","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-final","unit_id":"b2-u02","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Trabajo, liderazgo y negociación».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":1,"title_es":"Una sociedad que cambia","objective_es":"Hablar de cambios sociales, generaciones y costumbres.","intro":{"explanation":"Para hablar de cambios sociales: society (sociedad), generation (generación), trend (tendencia) y custom (costumbre). Ojo: custom no es «costume» (disfraz). Los cambios se cuentan con el present perfect: Technology has changed our society.","examples":[{"target":"Technology has changed our society.","base":"La tecnología cambió nuestra sociedad."},{"target":"Working from home is a growing trend.","base":"Trabajar desde casa es una tendencia en aumento."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de la sociedad, las generaciones y sus costumbres.","Describís tendencias con el present perfect."]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":2,"title_es":"Cifras y encuestas","objective_es":"Entender y contar datos: mayorías, promedios, aumentos y caídas.","intro":{"explanation":"Para dar cifras: the majority of (la mayoría de), a minority of (una minoría de), the average family (la familia promedio), one in four (uno de cada cuatro). Rise (rose, risen) es aumentar y decline, disminuir. Una survey es una encuesta.","examples":[{"target":"The population of the city has risen.","base":"La población de la ciudad aumentó."},{"target":"The majority of people voted for the plan.","base":"La mayoría de la gente votó a favor del plan."}]},"takeaways":["Entendés datos de una encuesta: majority, minority, average.","Contás aumentos y caídas con rise y decline."]},{"id":"b2-u03-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Una sociedad que cambia» y «Cifras y encuestas».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l03","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":4,"title_es":"Se dice que…","objective_es":"Contar lo que se dice, se cree o se espera con la pasiva impersonal.","intro":{"explanation":"Para contar lo que dice o piensa mucha gente, sin decir quién: It is said that… (se dice que), It is believed that… (se cree que). También con la persona o la cosa como sujeto: The homes are expected to be ready next year (se espera que estén listas). Algo widespread es muy extendido.","examples":[{"target":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","base":"Se dice que la casa tiene doscientos años."},{"target":"The new homes are expected to be ready next year.","base":"Se espera que las viviendas nuevas estén listas el año que viene."}]},"takeaways":["Contás lo que se dice o se cree: It is said that…","Contás lo que se espera: …is expected to…"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l04","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":5,"title_es":"Obras en marcha","objective_es":"Contar lo que se está haciendo y lo que ya se hizo con la pasiva.","intro":{"explanation":"Para algo que se está haciendo ahora: is / are being + participio (A new school is being built). Para algo que ya se hizo: has / have been + participio (The roof has been repaired). Take place es tener lugar, realizarse (un evento). Housing es la vivienda en general.","examples":[{"target":"A new school is being built near my house.","base":"Se está construyendo una escuela nueva cerca de mi casa."},{"target":"The festival will take place in the old market.","base":"El festival se va a realizar en el mercado viejo."}]},"takeaways":["Contás obras en marcha con is being + participio.","Contás lo que ya se hizo con has been + participio."]},{"id":"b2-u03-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Se dice que…» y «Obras en marcha».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l05","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":7,"title_es":"Una ciudad diversa","objective_es":"Hablar de la diversidad y opinar sobre lo que se debería hacer.","intro":{"explanation":"Diversity es la diversidad (de culturas, de idiomas, de edades). Para opinar sobre lo que habría que hacer sin decir quién: should be + participio (More homes should be built). También can be + participio para posibilidades: Many languages can be heard in the market.","examples":[{"target":"The diversity of the city is its best quality.","base":"La diversidad de la ciudad es su mejor cualidad."},{"target":"More homes should be built for young people.","base":"Deberían construirse más viviendas para los jóvenes."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de la diversidad de un lugar.","Opinás sobre lo que se debería hacer con should be + participio."]},{"id":"b2-u03-listen","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-words","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-final","unit_id":"b2-u03","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Sociedad, cultura y actualidad».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l01","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":1,"title_es":"En el laboratorio","objective_es":"Hablar de científicos, experimentos y pruebas.","intro":{"explanation":"A scientist hace research (investigación) y experiments. Evidence son las pruebas que demuestran algo: es incontable, así que se dice some evidence, no «an evidence». A discovery es un descubrimiento.","examples":[{"target":"The experiment failed, but we learned a lot.","base":"El experimento falló, pero aprendimos mucho."},{"target":"There is no evidence that it works.","base":"No hay pruebas de que funcione."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de experimentos, pruebas y descubrimientos.","Usás evidence como incontable: some evidence, no evidence."]},{"id":"b2-u04-l02","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":2,"title_es":"Un gran avance","objective_es":"Contar un invento o una idea nueva y quién la tuvo.","intro":{"explanation":"Come up with es idear, tener una idea: Who came up with this? A breakthrough es un avance clave. Invention es un invento e innovation, la innovación. Whose (cuyo) une a una persona con algo suyo: the scientist whose team won the prize.","examples":[{"target":"Who came up with this idea?","base":"¿A quién se le ocurrió esta idea?"},{"target":"She is the scientist whose team won the prize.","base":"Es la científica cuyo equipo ganó el premio."}]},"takeaways":["Contás quién tuvo una idea con come up with.","Unís una persona con algo suyo con whose."]},{"id":"b2-u04-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «En el laboratorio» y «Un gran avance».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":4,"title_es":"Información extra entre comas","objective_es":"Agregar información con oraciones de relativo explicativas y which.","intro":{"explanation":"Las explicativas van entre comas y dan información extra: The telephone, which was invented in 1876, … No se usa that. Which también puede retomar toda una idea: One experiment failed, which was frustrating (lo cual). Most of which y many of whom: la mayoría de los cuales, muchos de los cuales.","examples":[{"target":"One of our experiments failed, which was very frustrating.","base":"Uno de nuestros experimentos falló, lo cual fue muy frustrante."},{"target":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","base":"Tengo muchos libros, la mayoría de los cuales nunca leí."}]},"takeaways":["Agregás información extra entre comas con which y who.","Retomás toda una idea con which y hablás de partes con most of which."]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":5,"title_es":"Máquinas que piensan","objective_es":"Opinar sobre la inteligencia artificial, los datos y la privacidad.","intro":{"explanation":"Artificial intelligence (AI) es la inteligencia artificial. Data (datos) se usa casi siempre como incontable: the data is / are. Privacy es la privacidad. Rely on es depender de algo o confiar en que funcione: We rely on our phones.","examples":[{"target":"We rely on our phones for everything.","base":"Dependemos del teléfono para todo."},{"target":"I worry about my privacy online.","base":"Me preocupa mi privacidad en internet."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de la inteligencia artificial, los datos y la privacidad.","Decís de qué dependés con rely on."]},{"id":"b2-u04-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Información extra entre comas» y «Máquinas que piensan».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l05","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":7,"title_es":"Ponerse al día","objective_es":"Hablar de tecnología nueva y vieja y de cómo seguirle el ritmo.","intro":{"explanation":"Keep up with es mantenerse al día, seguir el ritmo: It’s hard to keep up with technology. Algo outdated está anticuado; algo cutting-edge es de vanguardia. Con which podés agregar un comentario: My phone, which I bought ten years ago, still works.","examples":[{"target":"It's hard to keep up with technology.","base":"Es difícil mantenerse al día con la tecnología."},{"target":"The lab uses cutting-edge technology.","base":"El laboratorio usa tecnología de vanguardia."}]},"takeaways":["Contás si te cuesta seguirle el ritmo a la tecnología.","Describís algo como outdated o cutting-edge."]},{"id":"b2-u04-listen","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-words","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-final","unit_id":"b2-u04","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Ciencia, tecnología e innovación».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u05-l01","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":1,"title_es":"¿Me lo puedo permitir?","objective_es":"Hablar de ahorros, préstamos y deudas.","intro":{"explanation":"Afford es poder permitirse algo: I can’t afford it (no me alcanza). Savings son los ahorros; a loan, un préstamo (take out a loan = pedir un préstamo); debt, una deuda. The interest rate es la tasa de interés.","examples":[{"target":"I can't afford a new car right now.","base":"Ahora no me puedo permitir un auto nuevo."},{"target":"She took out a loan to buy a flat.","base":"Pidió un préstamo para comprarse un departamento."}]},"takeaways":["Decís si podés permitirte algo con afford.","Hablás de ahorros, préstamos, deudas e intereses."]},{"id":"b2-u05-l02","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":2,"title_es":"Gastar menos","objective_es":"Contar cómo ahorrar: recortar gastos, comprar usado y buscar ofertas.","intro":{"explanation":"Cut back on es gastar menos en algo: cut back on subscriptions. Second-hand es de segunda mano, usado. A bargain es una ganga. Para contar lo que hiciste para ahorrar usás el present perfect o el past simple, como siempre.","examples":[{"target":"We need to cut back on eating out.","base":"Tenemos que gastar menos en comer afuera."},{"target":"I bought a second-hand bike for fifty dollars.","base":"Compré una bici usada por cincuenta dólares."}]},"takeaways":["Contás en qué gastás menos con cut back on.","Hablás de compras usadas y de gangas."]},{"id":"b2-u05-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «¿Me lo puedo permitir?» y «Gastar menos».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u05-l03","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":4,"title_es":"Mandar a hacer","objective_es":"Explicar que otra persona te hace o te arregla algo: have something done.","intro":{"explanation":"Have / get + objeto + participio: alguien hace algo por vos. I had my phone repaired (me arreglaron el teléfono, no lo arreglé yo). I’m going to get my hair cut (me voy a cortar el pelo, en la peluquería). Compará: I repaired my phone = lo arreglé yo.","examples":[{"target":"I had my phone repaired last week.","base":"La semana pasada me arreglaron el teléfono."},{"target":"I'd like to have the screen replaced.","base":"Quisiera que me cambiaran la pantalla."}]},"takeaways":["Contás lo que te hacen con have / get + objeto + participio.","Distinguís I had it repaired de I repaired it."]},{"id":"b2-u05-l04","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":5,"title_es":"Comparar con matices","objective_es":"Comparar precios y calidad: by far, twice as, nowhere near.","intro":{"explanation":"By far refuerza un superlativo: by far the best (por lejos el mejor). Twice as … as es el doble: twice as expensive as. Nowhere near as … as es «ni de cerca tan… como». The …-er, the …-er: The older the phone, the less sense it makes (cuanto más viejo, menos sentido tiene). Value for money es la relación calidad-precio.","examples":[{"target":"This phone is twice as expensive as that one.","base":"Este teléfono es el doble de caro que ese."},{"target":"The cheap ones are nowhere near as good.","base":"Los baratos no son ni de cerca tan buenos."}]},"takeaways":["Comparás con by far, twice as… as y nowhere near as… as.","Hablás de la relación calidad-precio."]},{"id":"b2-u05-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Mandar a hacer» y «Comparar con matices».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u05-l05","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":7,"title_es":"Consumidores exigentes","objective_es":"Opinar sobre marcas y precios: ganga, robo, demasiado caro.","intro":{"explanation":"A consumer es un consumidor. A brand es una marca. Si algo es carísimo para lo que vale, es overpriced; si el precio es abusivo, a rip-off (¡qué robo!). Lo contrario: a bargain o good value for money.","examples":[{"target":"Ten dollars for a coffee? What a rip-off!","base":"¿Diez dólares por un café? ¡Qué robo!"},{"target":"The food was good, but overpriced.","base":"La comida era buena, pero demasiado cara."}]},"takeaways":["Opinás sobre marcas y precios como consumidor.","Decís si algo es una ganga, un robo o demasiado caro."]},{"id":"b2-u05-listen","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u05-words","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u05-final","unit_id":"b2-u05","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Economía, consumo y finanzas».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l01","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":1,"title_es":"Algo debe de haber pasado","objective_es":"Deducir qué pasó con must have, might have y can't have.","intro":{"explanation":"Para deducir algo del pasado: must have + participio (estás casi seguro: She must have lost her phone), might / could have (es posible: She might have been busy) y can’t have (estás casi seguro de que no: She can’t have forgotten). En la conversación suena «must’ve», «might’ve».","examples":[{"target":"You must have been very tired.","base":"Debés de haber estado muy cansado."},{"target":"He might have missed the bus.","base":"Puede que haya perdido el colectivo."}]},"takeaways":["Deducís lo que pasó con must have y can’t have.","Decís lo que es posible con might have."]},{"id":"b2-u06-l02","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":2,"title_es":"Lo que debería haber hecho","objective_es":"Lamentar y criticar el pasado con should have y could have.","intro":{"explanation":"Should have + participio: algo que era lo correcto y no pasó (I should have called you = debería haberte llamado). Shouldn’t have: algo que pasó y no tendría que haber pasado. Could have: una posibilidad que no se aprovechó (You could have told me = me lo podrías haber dicho). Si te sentís mal por algo que hiciste, te sentís guilty.","examples":[{"target":"I should have called you yesterday.","base":"Debería haberte llamado ayer."},{"target":"You could have told me earlier!","base":"¡Me lo podrías haber dicho antes!"}]},"takeaways":["Lamentás lo que hiciste o no hiciste con should / shouldn’t have.","Reprochás con could have y decís que te sentís culpable."]},{"id":"b2-u06-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Algo debe de haber pasado» y «Lo que debería haber hecho».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":4,"title_es":"Peleas y reconciliaciones","objective_es":"Contar una pelea, reconocer que exageraste y hacer las paces.","intro":{"explanation":"Fall out (with someone) es pelearse; make up, reconciliarse. Overreact es exagerar, reaccionar de más. Don’t take it personally: no te lo tomes como algo personal. Si alguien está upset, está molesto o dolido (no «enojado» del todo).","examples":[{"target":"I fell out with my best friend last week.","base":"La semana pasada me peleé con mi mejor amiga."},{"target":"They argued, but they made up the next day.","base":"Discutieron, pero al día siguiente se reconciliaron."}]},"takeaways":["Contás una pelea con fall out y una reconciliación con make up.","Reconocés que exageraste y pedís que no lo tomen como algo personal."]},{"id":"b2-u06-l04","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":5,"title_es":"Estados de ánimo","objective_es":"Hablar del humor, animar a alguien y contar que alguien te falló.","intro":{"explanation":"Mood es el humor: in a good / bad mood. Cheer up es animar (Cheer up! = ¡Arriba!) y cheer someone up, animar a alguien. Let someone down es fallarle, decepcionarlo. Grateful es agradecido; stubborn, terco.","examples":[{"target":"Don't talk to him now. He is in a bad mood.","base":"No le hables ahora. Está de mal humor."},{"target":"I trusted you, and you let me down.","base":"Confié en vos y me fallaste."}]},"takeaways":["Describís el humor de alguien y lo animás.","Decís que alguien te falló o que estás agradecido."]},{"id":"b2-u06-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Peleas y reconciliaciones» y «Estados de ánimo».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l05","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":7,"title_es":"Ponerse en el lugar del otro","objective_es":"Hablar de la empatía y de la confianza en uno mismo.","intro":{"explanation":"Empathy es entender cómo se siente otra persona: to put yourself in someone’s shoes (ponerse en su lugar). Self-confidence es la confianza en uno mismo. Para hablar de lo que alguien podría haber sentido: She might have felt alone.","examples":[{"target":"Empathy means understanding how others feel.","base":"Empatía significa entender cómo se sienten los demás."},{"target":"Learning a language gave me more self-confidence.","base":"Aprender un idioma me dio más confianza en mí mismo."}]},"takeaways":["Explicás qué es la empatía y cómo se practica.","Hablás de tu confianza en vos mismo."]},{"id":"b2-u06-listen","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-words","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-final","unit_id":"b2-u06","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Psicología y relaciones».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":1,"title_es":"Un planeta más caliente","objective_es":"Hablar del calentamiento global, las emisiones y sus consecuencias.","intro":{"explanation":"Global warming es el calentamiento global, causado sobre todo por las emissions (emisiones) de CO2. Tu carbon footprint es tu huella de carbono: cuánto contaminás con lo que hacés. Una consequence es una consecuencia: Floods are a consequence of global warming.","examples":[{"target":"Global warming is changing the weather.","base":"El calentamiento global está cambiando el clima."},{"target":"Eating less meat reduces your carbon footprint.","base":"Comer menos carne reduce tu huella de carbono."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás del calentamiento global y las emisiones.","Explicás tu huella de carbono y las consecuencias."]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":2,"title_es":"Sequías e inundaciones","objective_es":"Entender una noticia sobre sequías, inundaciones y escasez.","intro":{"explanation":"A drought es una sequía; a flood, una inundación. A shortage es la escasez o la falta de algo: a water shortage. A threat es una amenaza. Las noticias suelen usar el present perfect: There hasn’t been any rain for eight months.","examples":[{"target":"It is the worst drought in fifty years.","base":"Es la peor sequía en cincuenta años."},{"target":"There is a water shortage in three towns.","base":"Hay escasez de agua en tres pueblos."}]},"takeaways":["Entendés noticias sobre sequías, inundaciones y escasez.","Hablás de amenazas y consecuencias del clima extremo."]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Un planeta más caliente» y «Sequías e inundaciones».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":4,"title_es":"A pesar de todo","objective_es":"Contrastar ideas con despite, in spite of, even though y even if.","intro":{"explanation":"Despite e in spite of van con un sustantivo o con -ing: Despite the rain… / In spite of feeling tired… Even though va con una oración completa y es más enfático que although: Even though I was tired, I finished. Even if es «aun si»: el resultado no cambia aunque se cumpla la condición.","examples":[{"target":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","base":"A pesar de la lluvia, salimos a caminar."},{"target":"Even if it rains, the game will go ahead.","base":"Aun si llueve, el partido se va a jugar."}]},"takeaways":["Usás despite / in spite of con un sustantivo o -ing.","Usás even though y even if con una oración."]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":5,"title_es":"Energía y futuro","objective_es":"Hablar de soluciones: energía renovable, sostenibilidad y cómo enfrentar un problema.","intro":{"explanation":"Renewable energy es la energía renovable (solar, eólica). Sustainable es sostenible: que puede durar sin dañar el planeta. Tackle a problem es enfrentar o abordar un problema. Whereas (mientras que) compara dos cosas opuestas: Coal is cheap, whereas solar energy is clean.","examples":[{"target":"We need more renewable energy.","base":"Necesitamos más energía renovable."},{"target":"I love the city, whereas my brother prefers the country.","base":"A mí me encanta la ciudad, mientras que mi hermano prefiere el campo."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de energía renovable y de un futuro sostenible.","Comparás dos ideas opuestas con whereas."]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «A pesar de todo» y «Energía y futuro».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l05","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":7,"title_es":"Problemas globales","objective_es":"Hablar de la pobreza, las especies en peligro y por qué todo está conectado.","intro":{"explanation":"Poverty es la pobreza. An endangered animal está en peligro de extinción. Para relacionar problemas: X is connected to Y, X is a consequence of Y, X is a threat to Y. Y para no perder la esperanza: Despite these problems, there is good news.","examples":[{"target":"Poverty and the environment are connected.","base":"La pobreza y el medioambiente están relacionados."},{"target":"The panda is an endangered animal.","base":"El panda es un animal en peligro de extinción."}]},"takeaways":["Relacionás problemas globales: connected, consequence, threat.","Hablás de especies en peligro y de la pobreza."]},{"id":"b2-u07-listen","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-words","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-final","unit_id":"b2-u07","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Medioambiente y problemas globales».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u08-l01","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":1,"title_es":"Se volvió viral","objective_es":"Hablar de rumores y publicaciones virales y de cómo se difunde la desinformación.","intro":{"explanation":"Algo que go viral (went viral) se comparte muchísimo en poco tiempo. A rumor es un rumor; misinformation, la desinformación. Spread (spread, spread) es difundirse. Clickbait es un título engañoso pensado para que hagas clic.","examples":[{"target":"The video went viral in one day.","base":"El video se volvió viral en un día."},{"target":"Fake news spreads faster than the truth.","base":"Las noticias falsas se difunden más rápido que la verdad."}]},"takeaways":["Contás que algo se volvió viral y se difundió.","Reconocés rumores, desinformación y clickbait."]},{"id":"b2-u08-l02","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":2,"title_es":"Lo que dijo, con precisión","objective_es":"Contar lo que alguien afirmó, sugirió o advirtió.","intro":{"explanation":"Claim that es afirmar algo que puede no ser cierto. Suggest va con -ing o con that: She suggested checking the website. Warn someone (not) to es advertir: He warned me not to touch it. Insist on + -ing o insist that: She insisted on paying.","examples":[{"target":"She suggested checking the official website.","base":"Sugirió consultar la página oficial."},{"target":"He warned me not to touch the cables.","base":"Me advirtió que no tocara los cables."}]},"takeaways":["Contás lo que alguien afirmó o sugirió con claim y suggest.","Contás advertencias e insistencias con warn e insist."]},{"id":"b2-u08-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Se volvió viral» y «Lo que dijo, con precisión».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u08-l03","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":4,"title_es":"Acusar, negar, admitir","objective_es":"Contar acusaciones, negaciones y confesiones con su forma correcta.","intro":{"explanation":"Accuse someone of + -ing: They accused him of lying. Deny + -ing es negar haber hecho algo: He denied taking the money. Admit + -ing es reconocerlo: She admitted making a mistake. Refuse to + verbo es negarse a hacer algo: He refused to answer.","examples":[{"target":"They accused him of lying.","base":"Lo acusaron de mentir."},{"target":"She admitted making a mistake.","base":"Reconoció haberse equivocado."}]},"takeaways":["Contás acusaciones con accuse someone of + -ing.","Usás deny y admit con -ing y refuse con to."]},{"id":"b2-u08-l04","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":5,"title_es":"Fuentes confiables","objective_es":"Distinguir fuentes confiables, parciales y engañosas.","intro":{"explanation":"A reliable source es una fuente confiable. Un artículo biased es parcial: muestra un solo lado. Misleading es engañoso (no siempre falso, pero lleva a una idea equivocada). Fact-check es verificar los datos.","examples":[{"target":"Is this a reliable source?","base":"¿Es una fuente confiable?"},{"target":"Always fact-check a story before you share it.","base":"Verificá siempre una noticia antes de compartirla."}]},"takeaways":["Evaluás si una fuente es confiable o parcial.","Detectás números y títulos engañosos y verificás antes de compartir."]},{"id":"b2-u08-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Acusar, negar, admitir» y «Fuentes confiables».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u08-l05","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":7,"title_es":"Los medios y su público","objective_es":"Opinar sobre los medios y contar una noticia con verbos de reporte.","intro":{"explanation":"The audience es el público de un programa, un medio o un espectáculo. Para contar una noticia con precisión, combinás los verbos de la unidad: The mayor denied the rumor, admitted that…, insisted that…, warned people not to…","examples":[{"target":"The program has a large audience.","base":"El programa tiene mucho público."},{"target":"The mayor denied the rumor about the park.","base":"La alcaldesa negó el rumor sobre el parque."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás del público de los medios.","Contás una noticia combinando claim, deny, admit, insist y warn."]},{"id":"b2-u08-listen","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u08-words","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u08-final","unit_id":"b2-u08","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Medios y desinformación».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l01","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":1,"title_es":"Si hubiera…","objective_es":"Imaginar un pasado distinto con el tercer condicional.","intro":{"explanation":"El tercer condicional habla de algo que no pasó y de su resultado imaginario: If + had + participio, would have + participio. If I had studied, I would have passed (si hubiera estudiado, habría aprobado; pero no estudié). En la conversación: If I’d studied, I’d have passed.","examples":[{"target":"If I had studied, I would have passed the exam.","base":"Si hubiera estudiado, habría aprobado el examen."},{"target":"If I hadn't left, I wouldn't have started my business.","base":"Si no me hubiera ido, no habría empezado mi negocio."}]},"takeaways":["Imaginás otro resultado para el pasado con if + had + participio.","Usás would have / wouldn’t have + participio en la otra parte."]},{"id":"b2-u09-l02","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":2,"title_es":"Ojalá hubiera…","objective_es":"Lamentar el pasado con if only y wish, y recordar una época.","intro":{"explanation":"Para lamentar algo del pasado: I wish / If only + past perfect. If only I had asked for help (ojalá hubiera pedido ayuda). I wish I hadn’t said that (ojalá no hubiera dicho eso). Look back on es recordar una época de tu vida. Struggle es tener dificultades con algo.","examples":[{"target":"If only I had asked for help.","base":"Ojalá hubiera pedido ayuda."},{"target":"I often look back on my school days.","base":"Muchas veces recuerdo mis años de colegio."}]},"takeaways":["Lamentás el pasado con if only / I wish + past perfect.","Recordás una época con look back on y contás qué te costaba."]},{"id":"b2-u09-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Si hubiera…» y «Ojalá hubiera…».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l03","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":4,"title_es":"La forma de pensar","objective_es":"Hablar de la mentalidad, la motivación y el progreso.","intro":{"explanation":"Your mindset es tu forma de pensar. Potential es tu potencial: reach your potential (desarrollarlo al máximo). Motivation es la motivación. Make progress es progresar (progress es incontable: no se dice «a progress»).","examples":[{"target":"Your mindset is more important than your talent.","base":"Tu forma de pensar es más importante que tu talento."},{"target":"You are making great progress with your English.","base":"Estás progresando mucho con tu inglés."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de la mentalidad y la motivación.","Contás tu progreso con make progress."]},{"id":"b2-u09-l04","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":5,"title_es":"Estudiar con método","objective_es":"Contar cómo organizás el estudio y cómo dejar de postergar.","intro":{"explanation":"Procrastinate es postergar, dejar todo para después. Self-discipline es la autodisciplina, la constancia. Keep track of es llevar la cuenta o el registro de algo. Catch up es ponerse al día: I need to catch up with the classes I missed.","examples":[{"target":"Learning a language takes self-discipline.","base":"Aprender un idioma requiere autodisciplina."},{"target":"I missed two classes, so I need to catch up.","base":"Falté a dos clases, así que tengo que ponerme al día."}]},"takeaways":["Contás cómo organizás tu estudio y llevás la cuenta.","Hablás de postergar, de la constancia y de ponerte al día."]},{"id":"b2-u09-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «La forma de pensar» y «Estudiar con método».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-l05","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":7,"title_es":"Salir de la zona de confort","objective_es":"Hablar de becas, inscripciones y de animarte a probar algo nuevo.","intro":{"explanation":"A scholarship es una beca. Enroll (in a course) es inscribirse. Your comfort zone es tu zona de confort, y step out of it, salir de ella. Give it a try es probarlo, animarse. Con el tercer condicional contás lo que habría pasado: If I’d known, I wouldn’t have…","examples":[{"target":"She won a scholarship to study abroad.","base":"Ganó una beca para estudiar en el exterior."},{"target":"You've never tried yoga? Give it a try!","base":"¿Nunca probaste yoga? ¡Probalo!"}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de becas e inscripciones.","Animás a alguien a probar algo fuera de su zona de confort."]},{"id":"b2-u09-listen","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-words","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u09-final","unit_id":"b2-u09","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Educación y desarrollo personal».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l01","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":1,"title_es":"Sumar argumentos","objective_es":"Agregar razones y consecuencias en un debate.","intro":{"explanation":"En un debate o un texto formal, moreover y furthermore suman otra razón (además, asimismo); van al principio de la oración, seguidos de coma. As a result introduce la consecuencia. Son más formales que also y so.","examples":[{"target":"The plan is cheap. Moreover, it is easy to start.","base":"El plan es barato. Además, es fácil de empezar."},{"target":"It rained all week. As a result, the match was canceled.","base":"Llovió toda la semana. Como resultado, se canceló el partido."}]},"takeaways":["Sumás argumentos con moreover y furthermore.","Presentás consecuencias con as a result."]},{"id":"b2-u10-l02","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":2,"title_es":"Lo que importa es…","objective_es":"Enfatizar una idea con oraciones escindidas.","intro":{"explanation":"Para poner el foco en una idea: What + sujeto + verbo + is… (What matters is that you tried; What worries me is the cost). The reason why + oración + is that… También It is / was… that…: It is the cost of ignorance that should worry us. In other words reformula lo dicho (o sea, es decir).","examples":[{"target":"What matters is that you tried.","base":"Lo que importa es que lo intentaste."},{"target":"The reason why I called is that I need your help.","base":"La razón por la que llamé es que necesito tu ayuda."}]},"takeaways":["Enfatizás con What… is y The reason why… is that…","Reformulás una idea con in other words."]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Sumar argumentos» y «Lo que importa es…».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l03","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":4,"title_es":"Reconocer y rebatir","objective_es":"Reconocer el punto del otro y responder con tu postura.","intro":{"explanation":"Un buen argumento reconoce la otra postura antes de rebatirla. Admittedly (es cierto que…) concede un punto; nevertheless (aun así) vuelve a tu postura. On the contrary (al contrario) dice que es todo lo opuesto. Your point of view es tu punto de vista.","examples":[{"target":"Admittedly, it is expensive.","base":"Es cierto que es caro."},{"target":"I'm not tired. On the contrary, I feel great.","base":"No estoy cansado. Al contrario, me siento genial."}]},"takeaways":["Concedés un punto con admittedly y lo rebatís con nevertheless.","Decís que es todo lo contrario con on the contrary."]},{"id":"b2-u10-l04","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":5,"title_es":"Argumentos sólidos","objective_es":"Evaluar si un argumento es válido y convincente.","intro":{"explanation":"A valid point es un argumento válido; convincing, convincente. An assumption es una suposición que no se demostró. Take into account es tener en cuenta: We need to take the costs into account (fijate que el objeto puede ir en el medio).","examples":[{"target":"That's just an assumption. Where is the evidence?","base":"Eso es sólo una suposición. ¿Dónde están las pruebas?"},{"target":"We need to take the costs into account.","base":"Tenemos que tener en cuenta los costos."}]},"takeaways":["Evaluás argumentos: valid, convincing, assumption.","Pedís que se tenga algo en cuenta con take into account."]},{"id":"b2-u10-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Reconocer y rebatir» y «Argumentos sólidos».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-l05","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":7,"title_es":"Sacar una conclusión","objective_es":"Cerrar un argumento: pesar pros y contras y resumir.","intro":{"explanation":"Outweigh es pesar más que algo: The benefits outweigh the costs. Para cerrar: To sum up (en resumen) o All things considered (en definitiva, considerando todo). Y una escindida da fuerza al final: It is the cost of ignorance that should worry us.","examples":[{"target":"The benefits outweigh the costs.","base":"Los beneficios superan a los costos."},{"target":"To sum up, I think the plan is a good idea.","base":"En resumen, creo que el plan es una buena idea."}]},"takeaways":["Comparás pros y contras con outweigh.","Concluís con to sum up y all things considered."]},{"id":"b2-u10-listen","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-words","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u10-final","unit_id":"b2-u10","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Argumentación y debate».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u11-l01","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":1,"title_es":"Comentar un libro","objective_es":"Hablar de una novela: la trama, los personajes y los capítulos.","intro":{"explanation":"A novel es una novela (no «una telenovela»). The plot es la trama; a character, un personaje (no el carácter de una persona); a chapter, un capítulo. Para opinar: The plot is clever, I couldn’t stop reading, My favorite character is…","examples":[{"target":"I could not stop reading the novel.","base":"No podía dejar de leer la novela."},{"target":"My favorite character is the old fisherman.","base":"Mi personaje favorito es el viejo pescador."}]},"takeaways":["Comentás una novela: trama, personajes y capítulos.","Das tu opinión sobre un libro."]},{"id":"b2-u11-l02","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":2,"title_es":"Giros inesperados","objective_es":"Hablar del narrador, de los giros de una historia y de cómo resultó todo.","intro":{"explanation":"The narrator es quien cuenta la historia. A twist es un giro inesperado. Turn out es resultar: It turns out that… (resulta que…). Set off es salir, ponerse en camino: She set off on foot.","examples":[{"target":"It turned out that we lived on the same street.","base":"Resultó que vivíamos en la misma calle."},{"target":"We set off early in the morning.","base":"Salimos temprano a la mañana."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás del narrador y de los giros de una historia.","Contás cómo resultó algo con turn out y cuándo salieron con set off."]},{"id":"b2-u11-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Comentar un libro» y «Giros inesperados».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u11-l03","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":4,"title_es":"Contar con estilo","objective_es":"Contar una historia con oraciones con participio y expresiones vivas.","intro":{"explanation":"Con un participio resumís una acción del mismo sujeto: Walking past the lighthouse, she noticed a light (mientras pasaba…). Having + participio cuenta lo que pasó antes: Having missed the train, she walked. Expresiones que dan vida a un relato: out of the blue (de la nada), break the ice (romper el hielo), burst into tears (ponerse a llorar).","examples":[{"target":"Having missed the last train, Elena set off on foot.","base":"Como había perdido el último tren, Elena salió a pie."},{"target":"My old friend called me out of the blue.","base":"Mi viejo amigo me llamó de la nada."}]},"takeaways":["Unís acciones con un participio: Walking…, Having…","Contás con expresiones como out of the blue y burst into tears."]},{"id":"b2-u11-l04","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":5,"title_es":"Nunca había visto algo así","objective_es":"Dar dramatismo a un relato con la inversión.","intro":{"explanation":"En los relatos, si empezás con never, hardly, no sooner o little, se invierten el auxiliar y el sujeto: Never had she felt so alone (= She had never felt so alone). Hardly had… when… y No sooner had… than…: una cosa pasó apenas terminó la otra. Little did I know…: poco me imaginaba.","examples":[{"target":"Never had she felt so alone.","base":"Nunca se había sentido tan sola."},{"target":"No sooner had we arrived than it started to rain.","base":"No bien llegamos, empezó a llover."}]},"takeaways":["Invertís auxiliar y sujeto después de never, hardly y no sooner.","Anticipás un giro con Little did I know…"]},{"id":"b2-u11-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Contar con estilo» y «Nunca había visto algo así».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u11-l05","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":7,"title_es":"Expresiones de todos los días","objective_es":"Entender y usar expresiones idiomáticas frecuentes.","intro":{"explanation":"Las expresiones idiomáticas no se traducen palabra por palabra. A piece of cake es pan comido; once in a blue moon, muy de vez en cuando; the last straw, la gota que rebalsó el vaso. Usalas en situaciones informales y con moderación.","examples":[{"target":"The exam was a piece of cake.","base":"El examen fue pan comido."},{"target":"I only go to the cinema once in a blue moon.","base":"Voy al cine muy de vez en cuando."}]},"takeaways":["Entendés expresiones idiomáticas frecuentes.","Usás algunas en situaciones informales."]},{"id":"b2-u11-listen","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u11-words","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u11-final","unit_id":"b2-u11","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Historias, libros y expresiones».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":1,"title_es":"Un dilema","objective_es":"Contar un dilema y pesar los pros y los contras.","intro":{"explanation":"A dilemma es un dilema: dos opciones difíciles. Weigh up es sopesar, evaluar: I’m weighing up the pros and cons (los pros y los contras). A trade-off es lo que perdés a cambio de lo que ganás: More money, less free time.","examples":[{"target":"I am weighing up the pros and cons.","base":"Estoy sopesando los pros y los contras."},{"target":"More money, less free time: that is the trade-off.","base":"Más plata, menos tiempo libre: ése es el costo."}]},"takeaways":["Contás un dilema y sopesás los pros y los contras.","Explicás lo que se pierde a cambio con trade-off."]},{"id":"b2-u12-l02","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":2,"title_es":"Si hubiera… ahora estaría…","objective_es":"Imaginar tu presente con otras decisiones: condicionales mixtos.","intro":{"explanation":"Condicional mixto 1: un pasado distinto cambia el presente. If + past perfect, would + verbo: If you had taken the job, you would be in Berlin now. Condicional mixto 2: un presente distinto habría cambiado el pasado. If + past simple, would have + participio: If I were braver, I would have said yes. Gut feeling es la intuición; have second thoughts, dudar.","examples":[{"target":"If you had taken the job, you'd be speaking German by now.","base":"Si hubieras aceptado el trabajo, ya estarías hablando alemán."},{"target":"If I were braver, I would have said yes.","base":"Si fuera más valiente, habría dicho que sí."}]},"takeaways":["Imaginás tu presente con un pasado distinto: If I had…, I would be…","Hablás de tu intuición y de tus dudas."]},{"id":"b2-u12-rev1","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":3,"title_es":"Repaso 1","objective_es":"Consolidar «Un dilema» y «Si hubiera… ahora estaría…».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l03","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":4,"title_es":"Resolver un conflicto","objective_es":"Hablar de un conflicto, de no tomar partido y de buscar puntos en común.","intro":{"explanation":"A conflict es un conflicto; resolve, resolverlo. A mediator ayuda a las dos partes sin take sides (tomar partido). La idea es find common ground: encontrar puntos en común.","examples":[{"target":"We can help you resolve the conflict.","base":"Podemos ayudarte a resolver el conflicto."},{"target":"Try to find some common ground.","base":"Tratá de encontrar puntos en común."}]},"takeaways":["Hablás de un conflicto y de cómo resolverlo.","Proponés no tomar partido y buscar puntos en común."]},{"id":"b2-u12-l04","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":5,"title_es":"Defender lo tuyo","objective_es":"Defender a tu equipo o tu postura y decidir cuándo ceder.","intro":{"explanation":"Stand up for es defender a alguien o algo: I have to stand up for my team. Back down es ceder, echarse atrás. Something is at stake: está en juego. Neither side (ninguna de las dos partes) va con el verbo en afirmativo: Neither side wanted to back down.","examples":[{"target":"I have to stand up for my team.","base":"Tengo que defender a mi equipo."},{"target":"Neither side wanted to back down.","base":"Ninguna de las dos partes quería ceder."}]},"takeaways":["Defendés a alguien con stand up for.","Hablás de lo que está en juego y de ceder con back down."]},{"id":"b2-u12-rev2","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":6,"title_es":"Repaso 2","objective_es":"Consolidar «Resolver un conflicto» y «Defender lo tuyo».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l05","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":7,"title_es":"Énfasis formal","objective_es":"Usar la inversión enfática en textos formales.","intro":{"explanation":"En avisos, correos formales y discursos: Not only + auxiliar + sujeto…, but (also)… (Not only is it free, but it is also confidential). Under no circumstances + auxiliar + sujeto (bajo ninguna circunstancia). Only then + auxiliar + sujeto (sólo entonces). Should you + verbo = If you + verbo, más formal: Should you need help, call reception.","examples":[{"target":"Not only is the service free, but it is also confidential.","base":"El servicio no sólo es gratuito, sino que también es confidencial."},{"target":"Should you need help, please call reception.","base":"Si necesita ayuda, llame a recepción."}]},"takeaways":["Enfatizás con Not only…, Under no circumstances… y Only then…","Escribís condiciones formales con Should you…"]},{"id":"b2-u12-listen","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":8,"title_es":"Práctica de escucha","objective_es":"Reconocer de oído las palabras y frases de la unidad.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-words","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":9,"title_es":"Palabras de la unidad","objective_es":"Fijar el vocabulario de la unidad: reconocerlo y escribirlo.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-final","unit_id":"b2-u12","position":10,"title_es":"Repaso final","objective_es":"Demostrar todo lo de «Decisiones y conflictos».","intro":null,"takeaways":[]}],"exercises":[{"id":"b2-u01-l01-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l01","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"misunderstanding","right":"malentendido"},{"left":"tone","right":"tono"},{"left":"actually","right":"en realidad"},{"left":"get across","right":"transmitir / hacer entender (una idea)"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-misunderstanding","en-tone","en-actually","en-get-across"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l01-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l01","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Sorry, I didn't ___ to wake you up.","translation":"Perdón, no quise despertarte.","options":["mean","want","try","think"]},"answer":"mean","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Didn’t mean to + verbo: no era tu intención hacerlo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-mean-to"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l01-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I thought he was angry, but ___ he was just tired.","translation":"Pensé que estaba enojado, pero en realidad sólo estaba cansado.","options":["actually","probably","finally","eventually"]},"answer":"actually","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Actually = en realidad (corrige lo que pensabas). No es «actualmente».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-actually"]},{"id":"b2-u01-l01-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-email-tone","setting":"Dos compañeros de trabajo hablan de un correo que cayó mal.","speakers":[{"name":"Nina","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sam","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Can I ask you something? Did my email this morning seem rude to you?"},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Honestly? It was a bit short. You just wrote \"Fix this today.\" No hello, no thanks."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Oh no. I didn't mean to sound angry. I was in a hurry, that's all."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"I know, but Mark actually thought you were annoyed with him."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"That's a misunderstanding. I'll call him and explain."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Good idea. A call is better than another email. Tone doesn't always get across in writing."}]},"question":"¿Por qué el correo de Nina pareció maleducado?","options":["Porque era muy corto, sin saludo ni agradecimiento","Porque tenía errores","Porque lo mandó a todos","Porque estaba en mayúsculas"]},"answer":"Porque era muy corto, sin saludo ni agradecimiento","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Sam dice: «It was a bit short. You just wrote \"Fix this today.\" No hello, no thanks».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-email-tone","setting":"Dos compañeros de trabajo hablan de un correo que cayó mal.","speakers":[{"name":"Nina","voice":"a"},{"name":"Sam","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Can I ask you something? Did my email this morning seem rude to you?"},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Honestly? It was a bit short. You just wrote \"Fix this today.\" No hello, no thanks."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"Oh no. I didn't mean to sound angry. I was in a hurry, that's all."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"I know, but Mark actually thought you were annoyed with him."},{"speaker":"Nina","text":"That's a misunderstanding. I'll call him and explain."},{"speaker":"Sam","text":"Good idea. A call is better than another email. Tone doesn't always get across in writing."}]},"question":"¿Qué cree Sam que conviene hacer?","options":["Llamar a Mark, porque el tono no siempre se entiende por escrito","Mandarle otro correo a Mark","No decir nada","Hablar con el jefe"]},"answer":"Llamar a Mark, porque el tono no siempre se entiende por escrito","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Sam dice: «A call is better than another email. Tone doe