itle":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Según el texto, ¿cuál es el problema de las indirectas?","options":["Que es fácil no darse cuenta de ellas","Que son maleducadas","Que llevan mucho tiempo","Que siempre ofenden"]},"answer":"Que es fácil no darse cuenta de ellas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «The problem is that hints are easy to miss».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de un blog sobre cómo dar una opinión difícil.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"¿Qué diferencia hace el texto entre straightforward y blunt?","options":["Se puede ser claro sin ser brusco","Son lo mismo","Ser brusco funciona mejor","Hay que evitar ser claro"]},"answer":"Se puede ser claro sin ser brusco","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «Being straightforward does not mean being blunt».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Una publicación de un blog sobre cómo dar una opinión difícil.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"¿Qué es lo que, según el texto, la gente acepta peor?","options":["El sarcasmo","Una opinión sincera","Un comentario positivo","Una solución en conjunto"]},"answer":"El sarcasmo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El texto dice: «people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u01-l04-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u01-l04","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","options":["Don't bring up politics at dinner.","Don't bring up politics at work.","Do bring up politics at dinner.","Don't talk about politics at dinner."]},