ions":["compromise","deal","proposal","contract"]},"answer":"compromise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Compromise no es «compromiso» (promesa): es una concesión, un punto medio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-supplier","setting":"Una gerente negocia con un proveedor el precio y la fecha de entrega.","speakers":[{"name":"Rachel","voice":"a"},{"name":"Daniel","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Rachel","text":"Thanks for the proposal, Daniel. To be honest, the price is higher than we expected."},{"speaker":"Daniel","text":"I understand. What if we kept the price but delivered two weeks earlier?"},{"speaker":"Rachel","text":"Time is not our main priority. The budget is. Could you go down five percent?"},{"speaker":"Daniel","text":"Five is difficult. I could offer three, as long as you sign a two-year contract."},{"speaker":"Rachel","text":"Two years is a long time. Let's meet halfway: four percent and an eighteen-month contract."},{"speaker":"Daniel","text":"That sounds fair. Provided that my director agrees, we have a deal."},{"speaker":"Rachel","text":"Great. Please send me the new terms in writing."}]},"question":"¿Cómo terminan cediendo los dos?","options":["Un cuatro por ciento de descuento y un contrato de dieciocho meses","Un cinco por ciento y dos años","Un tres por ciento y un año","Sin descuento y entrega antes"]},"answer":"Un cuatro por ciento de descuento y un contrato de dieciocho meses","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rachel propone: «Let’s meet halfway: four percent and an eighteen-month contract», y Daniel acepta.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l02","position":5,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Our main priority is the customer.","options":["Our main priority is the customer.","Our main priority is the budget.","Our first priority is the customer.","Your main priority is the customer."]},"answer":"Our main priority is the customer.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-priority"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l02","position":6,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","boss","is","flexible","about","working","hours"],"translation":"Mi jefe es flexible con los horarios de trabajo."},"answer":"My boss is flexible about working hours.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-flexible"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l02","position":7,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What is more important for you, time or money? (el dinero es tu prioridad)","translation":"¿Qué es más importante para vos, el tiempo o el dinero?"},"answer":"Money is my priority.","accepted_answers":["Money is my main priority.","My priority is money.","Money is my priority, not time."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-priority"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l02-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l02","position":8,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Nadie consiguió todo, pero fue un buen término medio."},"answer":"Nobody got everything, but it was a good compromise.","accepted_answers":["Nobody got everything but it was a good compromise.","No one got everything, but it was a good compromise."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":1,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"reach an agreement","options":["reach an agreement","priority","provided that","negotiate"]},"answer":"reach an agreement","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-reach-an-agreement"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":2,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Escribí la palabra completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"p_o_o_a_","hint":"propuesta"},"answer":"proposal","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["en-proposal"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":3,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Nadie consiguió todo, pero fue un buen término medio."},"answer":"Nobody got everything, but it was a good compromise.","accepted_answers":["Nobody got everything but it was a good compromise.","No one got everything, but it was a good compromise."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":4,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «meet halfway»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"meet halfway","options":["ceder cada uno un poco / encontrarse a mitad de camino","flexible","llegar a un acuerdo","carga de trabajo"]},"answer":"ceder cada uno un poco / encontrarse a mitad de camino","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-meet-halfway"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":5,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Nobody got everything, but it was a good ___.","translation":"Nadie consiguió todo, pero fue un buen término medio.","options":["compromise","deal","proposal","contract"]},"answer":"compromise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Compromise no es «compromiso» (promesa): es una concesión, un punto medio.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":6,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"So, do we agree on the price? (sí, trato hecho)","translation":"Entonces, ¿estamos de acuerdo con el precio?"},"answer":"Yes, we have a deal.","accepted_answers":["Yes, it's a deal.","Yes. We have a deal.","We have a deal."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-deal"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":7,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"If you agree, we have a ___.","translation":"Si estás de acuerdo, trato hecho.","options":["deal","proposal","price","meeting"]},"answer":"deal","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-deal"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":8,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"concesión / término medio"},"answer":"compromise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":9,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"meet halfway","right":"ceder cada uno un poco / encontrarse a mitad de camino"},{"left":"reach an agreement","right":"llegar a un acuerdo"},{"left":"proposal","right":"propuesta"},{"left":"compromise","right":"concesión / término medio"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-meet-halfway","en-reach-an-agreement","en-proposal","en-compromise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u02-rev1","position":10,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «deal»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"deal","options":["trato / acuerdo (comercial)","asumir / hacerse cargo de","rechazar","siempre que / mientras"]},"answer":"trato / acuerdo (comercial)","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-deal"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"You can borrow my car ___ you drive carefully.","translation":"Podés usar mi auto siempre que manejes con cuidado.","options":["as long as","in case","otherwise","although"]},"answer":"as long as","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"As long as + presente: la condición para que algo pase.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-as-long-as"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.","translation":"Llevá un paraguas por si llueve.","options":["in case","as long as","otherwise","unless"]},"answer":"in case","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In case: hacés algo antes, como precaución.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-in-case"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hurry up. ___, we will miss the train.","translation":"Apurate. Si no, vamos a perder el tren.","options":["Otherwise","Provided that","In case","As long as"]},"answer":"Otherwise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-otherwise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We will sign, provided that the price ___ the same.","translation":"Vamos a firmar, siempre y cuando el precio siga igual.","options":["stays","will stay","stayed","would stay"]},"answer":"stays","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Después de provided that (como después de if) va presente, aunque hables del futuro.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-provided-that"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Una candidata responde a una oferta de trabajo.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"¿Qué condición pone Laura para aceptar la oferta?","options":["Seguir trabajando dos días por semana desde su casa","Un sueldo más alto","Empezar el mes que viene","Tener su propio equipo"]},"answer":"Seguir trabajando dos días por semana desde su casa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura escribe: «I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Una candidata responde a una oferta de trabajo.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"¿Qué pasa si la empresa no acepta su condición?","options":["Laura va a rechazar la oferta","Laura va a aceptar igual","Laura va a pedir más tiempo","Laura va a hablar con su jefe actual"]},"answer":"Laura va a rechazar la oferta","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura escribe: «Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","options":["Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","Send me the terms in writing, as long as nothing changes.","Send me the terms by email, in case anything changes.","Send them the terms in writing, in case anything changes."]},"answer":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-in-case"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","will","help","you","as","long","as","you","help","me"],"translation":"Te voy a ayudar siempre que vos me ayudes."},"answer":"I will help you as long as you help me.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-as-long-as"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you taking a jacket? (por si hace frío)","translation":"¿Por qué llevás una campera?"},"answer":"In case it gets cold.","accepted_answers":["In case it's cold.","I am taking it in case it gets cold.","I'm taking a jacket in case it gets cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-in-case"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l03-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Apurate. Si no, vamos a perder el tren."},"answer":"Hurry up. Otherwise, we will miss the train.","accepted_answers":["Hurry up. Otherwise, we'll miss the train.","Hurry up. Otherwise we will miss the train.","Hurry up, otherwise we'll miss the train."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-otherwise"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"leader","right":"líder"},{"left":"delegate","right":"delegar"},{"left":"workload","right":"carga de trabajo"},{"left":"persuade","right":"convencer / persuadir"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-leader","en-delegate","en-workload","en-persuade"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She took ___ a new project last week.","translation":"La semana pasada asumió un proyecto nuevo.","options":["on","up","off","down"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-take-on"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I persuaded my boss ___ me a day off.","translation":"Convencí a mi jefe de que me diera un día libre.","options":["to give","giving","give","gave"]},"answer":"to give","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Persuade someone to + verbo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-persuade"]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Una líder de equipo habla con un empleado que está desbordado.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"¿Por qué Omar tiene tanto trabajo?","options":["Asumió un cliente nuevo y sigue con sus proyectos de antes","Un compañero renunció","Está aprendiendo un trabajo nuevo","Su jefa le dio los informes de Ben"]},"answer":"Asumió un cliente nuevo y sigue con sus proyectos de antes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Omar dice: «I took on the new client last month, and I’m still doing my old projects».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Una líder de equipo habla con un empleado que está desbordado.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"¿Qué solución propone Grace?","options":["Delegar los informes en Ben y ayudarlo al principio","Rechazar al cliente nuevo","Contratar a otra persona","Que Omar trabaje el fin de semana"]},"answer":"Delegar los informes en Ben y ayudarlo al principio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Grace dice: «Let’s delegate the reports to Ben… I’ll help him at the beginning».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de revista sobre el liderazgo.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"Según el artículo, ¿por qué conviene convencer en vez de dar órdenes?","options":["Porque un equipo que entiende la razón trabaja más para que la decisión funcione","Porque las órdenes son ilegales","Porque así el líder trabaja menos","Porque el equipo siempre tiene razón"]},"answer":"Porque un equipo que entiende la razón trabaja más para que la decisión funcione","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u02-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u02-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"A good leader listens to the team.","options":["A good leader listens to the team.","A good leader talks to the team.","A good leader listens to the client.","The good leaders listen to the team."]},"answer":"A good leader listens to the team.","accept