n_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-trend"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In some countries it is a ___ to take off your shoes at home.","translation":"En algunos países es costumbre sacarse los zapatos en casa.","options":["custom","trend","society","habit"]},"answer":"custom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Custom: costumbre de una sociedad. Habit: hábito de una persona.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-custom"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Según la socióloga, ¿qué dice cada generación de la siguiente?","options":["Que no respeta las costumbres de antes","Que es más trabajadora","Que vive mejor","Que es más feliz"]},"answer":"Que no respeta las costumbres de antes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El conductor pregunta si los jóvenes no respetan las costumbres y ella responde: «Every generation has said that about the next one».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Qué cambió y qué no, según la socióloga?","options":["Cambiaron las costumbres, pero no los valores","Cambiaron los valores, pero no las costumbres","No cambió nada","Cambió todo"]},"answer":"Cambiaron las costumbres, pero no los valores","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «Customs change, of course… But the values behind them haven’t disappeared».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Technology has changed our society.","options":["Technology has changed our society.","Technology will change our society.","Technology has changed our generation.","The internet has changed our society."]},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-society"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","generation","grew","up","with","the","internet"],"translation":"Mi generación creció con internet."},"answer":"My generation grew up with the internet.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-generation"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What is a big trend in your country? (trabajar desde casa)","translation":"¿Cuál es una gran tendencia en tu país?"},"answer":"Working from home is a big trend.","accepted_answers":["Working from home.","Working from home is a growing trend.","Working from home is a trend."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-trend"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l01-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"La tecnología cambió nuestra sociedad."},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":["Technology changed our society.","Technology's changed our society."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-society"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"population","right":"población"},{"left":"majority","right":"mayoría"},{"left":"minority","right":"minoría"},{"left":"survey","right":"encuesta"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-population","en-majority","en-minority","en-survey"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Prices have ___ a lot this year.","translation":"Los precios aumentaron mucho este año.","options":["risen","rose","rise","rised"]},"answer":"risen","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rise es irregular: rise, rose, risen. Con have va el participio: have risen.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-rise"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The ___ family has fewer than two children.","translation":"La familia promedio tiene menos de dos hijos.","options":["average","majority","minority","population"]},"answer":"average","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-average"]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre una encuesta acerca de las personas que viven solas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"¿Cómo cambió el número de hogares de una sola persona?","options":["Pasó de uno de cada diez a uno de cada cuatro","Pasó de uno de cada cuatro a uno de cada diez","No cambió","Bajó a la mitad"]},"answer":"Pasó de uno de cada diez a uno de cada cuatro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre una encuesta acerca de las personas que viven solas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"¿Qué dice la encuesta sobre la idea de que vivir solo hace sentir solo?","options":["Que la mayoría de quienes viven solos dicen ser felices","Que es cierta","Que sólo vale para los jóvenes","Que no lo preguntó"]},"answer":"Que la mayoría de quienes viven solos dicen ser felices","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l02-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre una encuesta acerca de las personas que viven solas.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"¿Qué disminuyó, según el artículo?","options":["El número de familias numerosas","El número de personas mayores","El número de hogares","El número de jóvenes"]},"answer":"El número de familias numerosas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «What has declined is the number of large families».","diffi