rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Cómo muestran hoy los jóvenes que les importa su familia, según la socióloga?","options":["De otra forma, por ejemplo con una videollamada en vez de un almuerzo","Ya no lo muestran","Viviendo con sus padres","Yendo a la iglesia"]},"answer":"De otra forma, por ejemplo con una videollamada en vez de un almuerzo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u03-l05-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u03-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un aviso de la municipalidad sobre el mercado viejo.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month."