pe":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u4-interview","setting":"Una entrevista de radio a una científica que inventó un filtro de agua.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mei","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"My guest today is Dr. Mei Lin, whose team has come up with a new way to clean water. Welcome."},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Thank you. Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"That sounds like a real breakthrough. How did you get the idea?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"By accident, actually. One of our experiments failed, which was very frustrating at the time. But the results showed something we didn't expect."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is there evidence that it works outside the lab?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Yes. We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water. The data are very clear."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What is the next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"¿Cómo son la mayoría de los pueblos donde probaron el filtro?","options":["No tienen agua limpia","Están cerca del laboratorio","Tienen mucho sol","Son muy grandes"]},"answer":"No tienen agua limpia","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mei dice: «We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u4-museum","document":"notice","setting":"Carteles de una sala de un museo de ciencia.","title":"Science Museum","lines":["Room 3: Ideas that changed the world","The telephone, which was invented in 1876, allowed people to talk across long distances for the first time.","Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes.","The World Wide Web was created by Tim Berners-Lee, a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment for his invention.","Which of these innovations do you use every day?"]},"question":"¿Por qué se recuerda a Marie Curie en el cartel?","options":["Sus descubrimientos cambiaron la medicina y ganó dos premios Nobel","Inventó el teléfono","Creó la World Wide Web","Fue la primera médica"]},"answer":"Sus descubrimientos cambiaron la medicina y ganó dos premios Nobel","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El cartel dice: «Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l03","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","options":["I have many books, most of which I have never read.","I have many books, all of which I have read.","I have some books, most of which I have never read.","I have many books, which I have never read."]},"answer":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-most-of-which"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l03","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","brother","who","lives","in","London","is","a","scientist"],"translation":"Mi hermano que vive en Londres es científico."},"answer":"My brother who lives in London is a scientist.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-scientist"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l03","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How did the experiment go? (falló, lo cual fue frustrante)","translation":"¿Cómo salió el experimento?"},"answer":"It failed, which was frustrating.","accepted_answers":["It failed, which was very frustrating.","The experiment failed, which was frustrating.","It failed which was frustrating."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-experiment"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l03","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Tengo muchos libros, la mayoría de los cuales nunca leí."},"answer":"I have many books, most of which I have never read.","accepted_answers":["I have many books, most of which I've never read.","I have a lot of books, most of which I have never read.","I have many books, most of which I never read."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-most-of-which"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"artificial intelligence","right":"inteligencia artificial"},{"left":"data","right":"datos"},{"left":"privacy","right":"privacidad"},{"left":"rely on","right":"depender de / confiar en"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-artificial-intelligence","en-data","en-privacy","en-rely-on"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We rely ___ our phones for everything.","translation":"Dependemos del teléfono para todo.","options":["on","in","of","for"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rely on (no «rely of»): depender de.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-rely-on"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The app collects ___ about your location.","translation":"La aplicación recoge datos sobre tu ubicación.","options":["data","privacy","evidence","innovation"]},"answer":"data","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-data"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u4-ai","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la inteligencia artificial.","title":"Who is watching the machines?","lines":["Artificial intelligence is everywhere: it chooses the songs we listen to, suggests the products we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"Según el autor, ¿cuál es «exactamente el problema»?","options":["Que dependemos de la IA todos los días sin pensarlo","Que la IA es muy cara","Que los médicos no la usan","Que la IA elige mal las canciones"]},"answer":"Que dependemos de la IA todos los días sin pensarlo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u4-ai","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la inteligencia artificial.","title":"Who is watching the machines?","lines":["Artificial intelligence is everywhere: it chooses the songs we listen to, suggests the products we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"¿Por qué la IA plantea preguntas sobre la privacidad?","options":["Porque necesita muchos datos, gran parte de nuestros teléfonos","Porque es muy lenta","Porque no funciona sin internet","Porque la usan los bancos"]},"answer":"Porque necesita muchos datos, gran parte de nuestros teléfonos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones… which raises serious questions about privacy».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u4-ai","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la inteligencia artificial.","title":"Who is watching the machines?","lines":["Artificial intelligence is everywhere: it chooses the songs we listen to, suggests the products we buy and even helps doctors read X-rays.","Most of us rely on it every day without thinking about it. That is exactly the problem.","To work well, these systems need huge amounts of data, much of which comes from our phones. Every search, every photo and every location can be stored, which raises serious questions about privacy.","This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data, how it is used and for how long it is kept.","Technology is a tool. Whether it helps or harms us depends on the rules we decide to give it."]},"question":"¿Cuál es la postura del autor sobre la innovación?","options":["No hay que rechazarla, pero hay que saber cómo se usan nuestros datos","Hay que prohibirla","No tiene ningún riesgo","Sólo deberían usarla los médicos"]},"answer":"No hay que rechazarla, pero hay que saber cómo se usan nuestros datos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «This does not mean we should reject innovation. But we should know who collects our data».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I worry about my privacy online.","options":["I worry about my privacy online.","I don't worry about my privacy online.","I worry about my data online.","I worried about my privacy online."]},"answer":"I worry about my privacy online.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-privacy"]},{"id":"b2-u04-l04-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u04-l04","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_word