 (con alguien)"},{"left":"make up","right":"reconciliarse / hacer las paces"},{"left":"overreact","right":"exagerar / reaccionar de más"},{"left":"take it personally","right":"tomárselo como algo personal"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-fall-out","en-make-up","en-overreact","en-take-it-personally"]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I fell ___ with my best friend last week.","translation":"La semana pasada me peleé con mi mejor amiga.","options":["out","up","down","off"]},"answer":"out","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-fall-out"]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"They argued, but they made ___ the next day.","translation":"Discutieron, pero al día siguiente se reconciliaron.","options":["up","out","down","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-make-up"]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Una columna de consejos: la carta de una lectora y la respuesta.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"¿Por qué se pelearon Lina y su amiga?","options":["La amiga llegó una hora tarde y Lina le gritó delante de todos","La amiga no fue al cumpleaños","Lina llegó tarde a una cena","La amiga le gritó a Lina"]},"answer":"La amiga llegó una hora tarde y Lina le gritó delante de todos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Lina escribe: «She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Una columna de consejos: la carta de una lectora y la respuesta.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"¿Cuál es la opinión de Ruth?","options":["Las dos se equivocaron: llegar tarde fue grosero, pero Lina exageró","Sólo se equivocó la amiga","Sólo se equivocó Lina","Ninguna se equivocó"]},"answer":"Las dos se equivocaron: llegar tarde fue grosero, pero Lina exageró","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ruth responde: «you both made mistakes… you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-advice","document":"post","setting":"Una columna de consejos: la carta de una lectora y la respuesta.","title":"Ask Ruth","lines":["Dear Ruth, Last week I fell out with my best friend. She was an hour late for my birthday dinner, and I shouted at her in front of everyone. Now I feel guilty, but I am also still a bit angry. What should I do? — Lina","Dear Lina, It sounds like you both made mistakes. Being an hour late is rude, and you had every right to be upset. However, you probably overreacted when you shouted at her in public.","Try not to take it personally. She could have had a good reason for being late. Call her, tell her how you felt, and listen to her side of the story.","Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up. — Ruth"]},"question":"¿Qué es lo más importante, según Ruth?","options":["Cómo se reconcilian, porque los amigos se pelean siempre","No pelearse nunca","Quién tiene razón","Que la amiga pida perdón primero"]},"answer":"Cómo se reconcilian, porque los amigos se pelean siempre","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ruth termina: «Friends fall out all the time. What matters is how you make up».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u06-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","options":["Don't take it personally. He is rude to everyone.","Don't take it personally. He is nice to everyone.","Take it personally. He i