er":"Empathy","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-empathy"]},{"id":"b2-u06-l05-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Learning a language gave me more ___.","translation":"Aprender un idioma me dio más confianza en mí mismo.","options":["self-confidence","empathy","mood","evidence"]},"answer":"self-confidence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-self-confidence"]},{"id":"b2-u06-l05-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u06-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast sobre psicología entrevista a un psicólogo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Según el psicólogo, ¿la empatía es lo mismo que estar de acuerdo?","options":["No: es entender cómo se siente 