tions":["footprint","step","warming","size"]},"answer":"footprint","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Extreme weather is a ___ of global warming.","translation":"El clima extremo es una consecuencia del calentamiento global.","options":["consequence","emissions","footprint","solution"]},"answer":"consequence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-consequence"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la huella de carbono.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"¿Cuál es la idea principal del artículo?","options":["Que los cambios individuales ayudan, pero no alcanzan sin cambios grandes","Que las duchas cortas salvan el planeta","Que no hay que hacer nada","Que las empresas no contaminan"]},"answer":"Que los cambios individuales ayudan, pero no alcanzan sin cambios grandes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «These things matter, but they are not enough» y propone el paso a la energía renovable.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la huella de carbono.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"¿Qué compara el autor con whereas?","options":["Lo que ahorra una familia con lo que produce una fábrica","Dos tipos de energía","Dos países","La carne y el pescado"]},"answer":"Lo que ahorra una familia con lo que produce una fábrica","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Global warming is changing the weather.","options":["Global warming is changing the weather.","Global warming is changing the world.","Global warming has changed the weather.","Pollution is changing the weather."]},"answer":"Global warming is changing the weather.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-global-warming"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Cars","produce","a","lot","of","emissions"],"translation":"Los autos producen muchas emisiones."},"answer":"Cars produce a lot of emissions.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-emissions"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How can you reduce your carbon footprint? (comer menos carne)","translation":"¿Cómo podés reducir tu huella de carbono?"},"answer":"I can eat less meat.","accepted_answers":["By eating less meat.","Eat less meat.","I can reduce it by eating less meat."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l01-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"El calentamiento global está cambiando el clima."},"answer":"Global warming is changing the weather.","accepted_answers":["Global warming is changing the climate.","Global warming's changing the weather."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-global-warming"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"drought","right":"sequía"},{"left":"flood","right":"inundación"},{"left":"shortage","right":"escasez / falta"},{"left":"threat","right":"amenaza"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-drought","en-flood","en-shortage","en-threat"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":2,"type":"image_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué muestra la imagen?","payload":{"type":"image_choice","emoji":"🏜️","options":["drought","flood","storm","snow"]},"answer":"drought","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-drought"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"There is a water ___ in three towns.","translation":"Hay escasez de agua en tres pueblos.","options":["shortage","drought","threat","flood"]},"answer":"shortage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-shortage"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un informe de radio sobre la sequía en una región agrícola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"¿Por qué los ríos siguen bajos?","options":["Porque las tormentas de la semana pasada no alcanzaron después de ocho meses sin lluvia","Porque los agricultores usan demasiada agua","Porque hubo inundaciones","Porque cerraron una represa"]},"answer":"Porque las tormentas de la semana pasada no alcanzaron después de ocho meses sin lluvia","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: «This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un informe de radio sobre la sequía en una región agrícola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"¿Qué tiene de irónico la situación, según Paula?","options":["Que hace dos años la misma región sufrió inundaciones terribles","Que nunca había llovido tanto","Que los agricultores ganaron más","Que los científicos no saben la causa"]},"answer":"Que hace dos años la misma región sufrió inundaciones terribles","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: «Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Un resumen de un informe de una organización ambiental.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"¿A quiénes afectan más las sequías y las inundaciones, según el informe?","options":["A los países más pobres, aunque son los que menos contaminan","A los países más ricos","A las grandes empresas","A todos por igual"]},"answer":"A los países más pobres, aunque son los que menos contaminan","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El informe dice: «Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The flood destroyed many homes.","options":["The flood destroyed many homes.","The flood destroyed many roads.","The storm destroyed many homes.","The floods destroyed a few homes."]},"answer":"The flood destroyed many homes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-flood"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (por la sequía)","translation":"¿Por qué no hay agua en el pueblo?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-drought"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l02-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l02","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Es la peor sequía en cincuenta años."},"answer":"It is the worst drought in fifty years.","accepted_answers":["It's the worst drought in fifty years.","This is the worst drought in fifty years.","It is the worst drought in 50 years."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-drought"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"There is a water ___ in three towns.","translation":"Hay escasez de agua en tres pueblos.","options":["shortage","drought","threat","flood"]},"answer":"shortage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-shortage"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":2,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «carbon footprint»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"carbon footprint","options":["huella de carbono","sequía","emisiones","calentamiento global"]},"answer":"huella de carbono","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"drought","options":["drought","endangered","even though","emissions"]},"answer":"drought","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-drought"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":4,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «flood»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"flood","options":["inundación","sequía","huella de carbono","escasez / falta"]},"answer":"inundación","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-flood"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":5,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"carbon footprint","right":"huella de carbono"},{"left":"drought","right":"sequía"},{"left":"global warming","right":"calentamiento global"},{"left":"consequence","right":"consecuencia"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-carbon-footprint","en-drought","en-global-warming","en-consequence"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":6,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (por la sequía)","translation":"¿Por qué no hay agua en el pueblo?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-drought"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":7,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"consecuencia"},"answer":"consequence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-consequence"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How can you reduce your carbon footprint? (comer menos carne)","translation":"¿Cómo podés reducir tu huella de carbono?"},"answer":"I can eat less meat.","accepted_answers":["By eating less meat.","Eat less meat.","I can reduce it by eating less meat."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":9,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Cars","produce","a","lot","of","emissions"],"translation":"Los autos producen muchas emisiones."},"answer":"Cars produce a lot of emissions.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-emissions"]},{"id":"b2-u07-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u07-rev1","position":10,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Escribí la palabra completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"g_o_a_ w_r_i_g","hint":"calentamiento global"},"answer":"global warming","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["en-global-warming"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ the rain, we went for a walk.","translation":"A pesar de la lluvia, salimos a caminar.","options":["Despite","Even though","Although","Even if"]},"answer":"Despite","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Despite + sustantivo (the rain). Even though y although van con una oración.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-despite"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ I was tired, I finished the report.","translation":"A pesar de que estaba cansado, terminé el informe.","options":["Even though","Despite","In spite of","Whereas"]},"answer":"Even though","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even though + oración completa (I was tired).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-even-though"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In spite ___ the price, I take the train.","translation":"Pese al precio, tomo el tren.","options":["of","to","for","that"]},"answer":"of","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In spite of (con of); despite va sin of.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-in-spite-of","en-tackle","en-sustainable"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ it rains, the game will go ahead.","translation":"Aun si llueve, el partido se va a jugar.","options":["Even if","Despite","Whereas","In spite of"]},"answer":"Even if","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-even-if"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Dos estudiantes discuten si una persona puede ayudar al planeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"¿Qué hace Noah a pesar del precio?","options":["Viaja en tren para visitar a su familia en vez de volar","Vuela menos de vacaciones","Usa la bici para ir a la facultad","Dejó de comer carne"]},"answer":"Viaja en tren para visitar a su familia en vez de volar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Noah dice: «I’ve stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Dos estudiantes discuten si una persona puede ayudar al planeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"¿Qué quiere decir Mia con «Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference»?","options":["Que aunque todos lo hicieran, el efecto sería muy pequeño","Que nadie va a dejar de volar","Que volar no contamina","Que la ciudad es muy chica"]},"answer":"Que aunque todos lo hicieran, el efecto sería muy pequeño","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even if: aun si todos dejaran de volar, el resultado (una diferencia mínima) no cambia.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un informe de radio sobre la sequía en una región agrícola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"¿Qué les pasó a los agricultores aunque redujeron el uso de agua?","options":["Muchos perdieron la mitad de sus cultivos","Ganaron más dinero","Se mudaron a otra región","No tuvieron problemas"]},"answer":"Muchos perdieron la mitad de sus cultivos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: «Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","options":["Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","Because I was tired, I finished the report.","Even though I was tired, I started the report.","Even though I was busy, I finished the report."]},"answer":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-even-though"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did you go to the beach? (sí, a pesar del frío)","translation":"¿Fueron a la playa?"},"answer":"Yes, despite the cold.","accepted_answers":["Yes, in spite of the cold.","Yes, we went despite the cold.","Yes, even though it was cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-despite"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l03-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"A pesar de la lluvia, salimos a caminar."},"answer":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","accepted_answers":["In spite of the rain, we went for a walk.","Despite the rain we went for a walk.","We went for a walk despite the rain."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-despite"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e01","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"renewable","right":"renovable"},{"left":"sustainable","right":"sostenible / sustentable"},{"left":"tackle","right":"abordar / enfrentar (un problema)"},{"left":"whereas","right":"mientras que"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-renewable","en-sustainable","en-tackle","en-whereas"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e02","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I love the city, ___ my brother prefers the country.","translation":"A mí me encanta la ciudad, mientras que mi hermano prefiere el campo.","options":["whereas","despite","even if","in spite of"]},"answer":"whereas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Whereas une dos hechos opuestos.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-whereas"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e03","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We need to ___ the real causes of the problem.","translation":"Tenemos que enfrentar las verdaderas causas del problema.","options":["tackle","reduce","produce","protect"]},"answer":"tackle","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Collocation: tackle a problem (enfrentar un problema).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-tackle"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e04","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo de opinión sobre la huella de carbono.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"¿Cuál es la verdadera solución, según el autor?","options":["Pasar rápido a la energía renovable, algo que sólo pueden hacer los gobiernos","Que cada familia tome duchas cortas","Cerrar todas las fábricas","Dejar de votar"]},"answer":"Pasar rápido a la energía renovable, algo que sólo pueden hacer los gobiernos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy… Only governments can make that happen».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Dos estudiantes discuten si una persona puede ayudar al planeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"¿En qué terminan de acuerdo Noah y Mia?","options":["Los dos quieren un futuro sostenible, pero no coinciden en cómo llegar","Los dos van a dejar de volar","No coinciden en nada","Mia acepta que una persona puede cambiar todo"]},"answer":"Los dos quieren un futuro sostenible, pero no coinciden en cómo llegar","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mia dice: «So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Dos estudiantes discuten si una persona puede ayudar al planeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"¿Qué causas quiere enfrentar Mia?","options":["El carbón, el petróleo y la forma de producir alimentos","Los vuelos y los trenes","Las duchas largas","Las grandes ciudades"]},"answer":"El carbón, el petróleo y la forma de producir alimentos","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mia dice: «we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We need more renewable energy.","options":["We need more renewable energy.","We need less renewable energy.","We need more clean energy.","We have more renewable energy."]},"answer":"We need more renewable energy.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-renewable"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["We","all","want","a","sustainable","future"],"translation":"Todos queremos un futuro sostenible."},"answer":"We all want a sustainable future.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-sustainable"]},{"id":"b2-u07-l04-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u07-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What kind of energy should we use? (energía renovable, como la solar)","translation":"¿Qué tipo de 