","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"¿Cuál es el dilema de Alice?","options":["Si aceptar un puesto en Lisboa y mudarse en un mes","Si cambiar de carrera","Si mudarse a Berlín","Si dejar su trabajo para cuidar a sus padres"]},"answer":"Si aceptar un puesto en Lisboa y mudarse en un mes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dice: «I’ve got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager… I’d have to move in a month».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e05","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre cómo tomar decisiones importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"Según el artículo, ¿por qué son difíciles las grandes decisiones?","options":["Porque siempre se gana algo a cambio de perder otra cosa","Porque nunca hay información","Porque la gente es insegura","Porque llevan mucho tiempo"]},"answer":"Porque siempre se gana algo a cambio de perder otra cosa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e06","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un artículo sobre cómo tomar decisiones importantes.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"¿Para qué sirve anotar los pros y los contras, según el artículo?","options":["Para sopesarlos con más calma","Para mostrárselos a otros","Para no tener que decidir","Para recordarlos años después"]},"answer":"Para sopesarlos con más calma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El artículo dice: «Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e07","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"I've got a real dilemma.","options":["I've got a real dilemma.","I've got a real problem.","I haven't got a real dilemma.","We've got a real dilemma."]},"answer":"I've got a real dilemma.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-dilemma"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e08","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Ordená las palabras","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Write","down","the","pros","and","cons"],"translation":"Anotá los pros y los contras."},"answer":"Write down the pros and cons.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["en-pros-and-cons"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e09","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Have you decided about the new job? (no, todavía estás sopesando los pros y los contras)","translation":"¿Decidiste lo del trabajo nuevo?"},"answer":"No, I'm still weighing up the pros and cons.","accepted_answers":["No, I am still weighing up the pros and cons.","I'm still weighing up the pros and cons.","Not yet. I'm still weighing up the pros and cons."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-weigh-up","en-pros-and-cons"]},{"id":"b2-u12-l01-e10","lesson_id":"b2-u12-l01","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traducí al inglés","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Tengo un verdadero dilema."},"answer":"I've got a real dilemma.","accepted_answers":