spect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Según la socióloga, ¿qué dice cada generación de la siguiente?","options":["Que no respeta las costumbres de antes","Que es más trabajadora","Que vive mejor","Que es más feliz"]},"answer":"Que no respeta las costumbres de antes","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"El conductor pregunta si los jóvenes no respetan las costumbres y ella responde: «Every generation has said that about the next one».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"en.ex.fefv2t4th4598p","content_hash":"v1:a286e78d44cb5f546a1f91912a0d2c8e77f068af0bd98919a93ad27b4da76a3b","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Qué cambió y qué no, según la socióloga?","options":["Cambiaron las costumbres, pero no los valores","Cambiaron los valores, pero no las costumbres","No cambió nada","Cambió todo"]},"answer":"Cambiaron las costumbres, pero no los valores","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «Customs change, of course… But the values behind them haven’t disappeared».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"en.ex.u5eulbbxi3bdne","content_hash":"v1:e48ceb5a3a8c8f4631375faf8c416507d48434d8fd86679ae9afefdc033ea353","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Technology has changed our society.","options":["Technology has changed our society.","Technology will change our society.","Technology has changed our generation.","The internet has changed our society."]},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"e