Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Para qué menciona la socióloga a los antiguos griegos?","options":["Para mostrar que la queja sobre los jóvenes es muy antigua","Para hablar de la historia de Grecia","Para decir que los griegos eran mejores","Para explicar una costumbre griega"]},"answer":"Para mostrar que la queja sobre los jóvenes es muy antigua","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"en.ex.xfe4w9hc8rjs4m","content_hash":"v1:bbb06dbf3c59c12dd46fd8f3939a9e80826f2bc4e39e96ff320c7c7fc6122403","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un pódcast entrevista a una socióloga sobre las generaciones.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"¿Qué opina la socióloga de la idea de que la distancia entre generaciones es cada vez mayor?","options":["Que mucha gente lo cree, pero su investigación no lo confirma","Que es cierta","Que es nueva","Que nadie la cree"]},"answer":"Que mucha gente lo cree, pero su investigación no lo confirma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: «Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things».","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"en.ex.fv0sbrtdmjk0zf","content_hash":"v1:b9cd9dad5897c8e669135498051d6a371153ae04c0582766ac167f8b92fdf20c","prompt_es":"Leé y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"en.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un aviso de la municipalidad sobre el mercado viejo.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed unti